  "goodToKnow": "Jedweder means any at all or every, a formal, emphatic version of jeder or jeglicher, mostly in negative contexts: ohne jedwede Hilfe, jedweder Kritik entzogen. It declines like dieser: jedwede Frau, jedwedes Kind. It's common in legal and official texts and sounds old-fashioned in speech, where jeder or irgendein are normal."
